## The finding

`crime_00064` — **Duplicate Component Shape**, medium / confidence 0.70, detector `duplicate_component_shape.js`:

> `div` subtree appears in 4 files with the same structural shape · hash `e96b55b64336…`

| File | Lines |
|---|---|
| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 142–150 |
| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 152–160 |
| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 101–109 |
| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 112–120 |

I read all four sites. The repeated subtree is the **form-actions footer** — the Cancel link + submit button row that closes every invoice form:

```tsx
<div className="mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4">
  <Link
    href="/dashboard/invoices"
    className="flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200"
  >
    Cancel
  </Link>
  <Button type="submit">Create Invoice</Button>   {/* only this text varies */}
</div>
```

All four copies are byte-identical except the submit label: `Create Invoice` (create forms) vs `Edit Invoice` (edit forms). The `href`, both className strings, and the ordering are the same in all four.

## Proposed shared component

`InvoiceFormActions` — a presentational component in each app's UI layer.

**New file (per app):** `app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`

```tsx
import Link from 'next/link';
import { Button } from '@/app/ui/button';

export interface InvoiceFormActionsProps {
  /** Submit button label — the only thing that differs between create and edit today. */
  submitLabel: string;
  /** Where Cancel navigates. Defaults to the invoices index. */
  cancelHref?: string;              // default: '/dashboard/invoices'
  /** Cancel link text. Defaults to 'Cancel'. */
  cancelLabel?: React.ReactNode;    // default: 'Cancel'
  /** Disables submit while a server action is in flight. */
  pending?: boolean;
  /** Slot: extra controls rendered left of Cancel (e.g. a Delete button). */
  children?: React.ReactNode;
}

export function InvoiceFormActions({
  submitLabel,
  cancelHref = '/dashboard/invoices',
  cancelLabel = 'Cancel',
  pending = false,
  children,
}: InvoiceFormActionsProps) {
  return (
    <div className="mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4">
      {children}
      <Link
        href={cancelHref}
        className="flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200"
      >
        {cancelLabel}
      </Link>
      <Button type="submit" aria-disabled={pending}>
        {submitLabel}
      </Button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Public API summary**

- **Props:** `submitLabel` (required, string) · `cancelHref` (optional, defaults `/dashboard/invoices`) · `cancelLabel` (optional, defaults `Cancel`) · `pending` (optional boolean)
- **Slots:** one — `children`, rendered as leading actions before Cancel. This is the escape hatch that stops the next form from copy-pasting the div again when it needs a third button.

`pending` maps onto the existing `Button`, which already styles `aria-disabled` (`aria-disabled:cursor-not-allowed aria-disabled:opacity-50` in `app/ui/button.tsx:12`) — so no change to `Button` is needed. `pending` is speculative today; drop it if you'd rather keep the API to exactly what the four call sites use.

